		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=42465#p42465"><![CDATA[
I haven’t been able to find any resources about simulating stepper motors or other types of motors. Minotaur has an example of a simple DC motor, with conversion of PWM to the applied torque, but that example actually does not use many of the constants meant to provide accurate simulation. <br><br>For background, I’m attempting to build a model for a reinforcement learning agent to train over before generalizing to a real life model, and would like this model to be as accurate as possible. <br><br>Are there any examples, resources, or support for simulating different motor types?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=13184">Gerard</a> — Mon Nov 11, 2019 3:49 pm</p><hr />
